      "content": "The database connection is persistently denied (authentication error), so I cannot execute verification queries. I'll base the final SQL entirely on the semantic-network evidence and the strong precedent metrics (dw_1833 for the FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY → FCLT_ORGANIZATION → FCLT_ROOMS join pattern with `DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL`; dw_4061 for `AREA > 40` room statistics with `AVG`/`MAX-MIN`/`VARIANCE`; dw_3664 and dw_4387 for the `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED` ⋈ `ACADEMIC_TERMS ON TERM_CODE` with `IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` pattern).\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n- **FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY**: bridge table mapping facilities organizations to DLC keys; one row per organization-DLC assignment; used to filter organizations with a non-null DLC key before room statistics (per its `desc` and dw_1833's `WHERE d.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL`).\n- **FCLT_ORGANIZATION**: facilities organization dimension; carries `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`, `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME` (\"Department name as recorded in HR systems\" — the department-name column named in the hint mapping), `DLC_KEY`, `DLC_NAME`.\n- **FCLT_ROOMS**: one row per physical room; `AREA` (square meters, \"used in area statistics (average, range, variance)\"), `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` for room-to-organization attribution.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED**: catalog-level subject offering per term/year; `DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `TOTAL_UNITS`, `TERM_CODE` (offering term, joins to term tables).\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS**: term dimension; `TERM_CODE`, `IS_REGULAR_TERM` ('Y' = Fall/Spring regular term) — the only term table carrying `IS_REGULAR_TERM` (ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL lacks it).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph on FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY: joins to FCLT_ORGANIZATION (incoming), MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY and FCLT_ROOMS (outgoing); member of `column_concept_dlc_key`.\n- FCLT_ROOMS ⋈ FCLT_ORGANIZATION via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (documented in both tables' column descs and used in dw_1833, dw_1465).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS via `TERM_CODE` (documented join key; used in dw_3664, dw_4387).\n- Cross-domain department link: `FCLT_ORGANIZATION.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME` = `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` (explicitly given in the hint column mapping; `column_concept_department_name` confirms the academic name domain of DEPARTMENT_NAME).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n- **Room source**: FCLT_ROOMS (area in m², organization assignment via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) vs FAC_ROOMS (FAC_* key family) vs SPACE_DETAIL (space-unit assignment, square footage). The hint's gold tables and join keys select FCLT_ROOMS; dw_1833/dw_1465/dw_4061 all compute room-area statistics from FCLT_ROOMS.\n- **Units source**: `column_concept_total_units` decision guide — \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance) over catalog offerings → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\". SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY are registrar alternatives, excluded by the gold-table list.\n- **Term table**: ACADEMIC_TERMS is the only one with `IS_REGULAR_TERM` (ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL explicitly lacks it), so \"regular academic terms\" ⇒ `ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'` joined on TERM_CODE (dw_3664/dw_4387 precedent uses TERM_CODE, not EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE).\n- **Fitness**: all atomic requirements (dept name, area avg/range/var with AREA>40 filter, units avg/range/var with regular-term filter) are SUPPORTED by the gold tables; no candidate violates any requirement.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- dw_1833: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY + FCLT_ORGANIZATION + FCLT_ROOMS with `DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL` for room-area STDDEV per organization/department.\n- dw_4061: AVG/MAX−MIN/VARIANCE of FCLT_ROOMS.AREA with `AREA > 40`.\n- dw_3664, dw_4387: AVG/VARIANCE of COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS on TERM_CODE with `IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'`, grouped by DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_ROOMS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, ACADEMIC_TERMS: `semantic_get` + graph traversal ✓\n- dw_4061, dw_1833, dw_1465, dw_3664, dw_4387: `semantic_get` (full SQL precedents) ✓\n- column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_dlc_key: retrieved ✓\n- concepts (room_space_inventory, facility_organization_dimension, subject_offering_facts, academic_term_dimension, dept_hr_org_hierarchy): descriptions reviewed from search results ✓\n- mysql_query: attempted 4 times — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\" (infrastructure issue); verification by execution was impossible.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n6a. Two aggregation CTEs joined on department name: room stats from FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY ⋈ FCLT_ORGANIZATION ⋈ FCLT_ROOMS (filter `DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL`, `AREA > 40`, group by `HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME`); unit stats from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS on TERM_CODE (filter `IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'`, group by `DEPARTMENT_NAME`). Range = MAX−MIN, variance = VARIANCE() — exactly as in dw_4061/dw_3664. No rounding.\n\n6b/6c. Join pattern, filters, and aggregate functions each follow a documented precedent (dw_1833 for the DLC-key bridge join; dw_4061 for AREA>40 statistics; dw_3664/dw_4387 for regular-term unit statistics); the cross-side department link uses HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME = DEPARTMENT_NAME per the hint mapping and `column_concept_department_name` (same academic name domain). Aggregating each side separately before joining avoids fan-out between rooms and subject offerings.\n\n6d. Caveat: database execution was unavailable, so join-match rates could not be empirically verified; the SQL follows the gold-table/join-key specification exactly.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_5ff805a955684e02ab7a97c0",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH room_stats AS (\\n    SELECT o.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME AS DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n           AVG(r.AREA) AS avg_area,\\n           MAX(r.AREA) - MIN(r.AREA) AS area_range,\\n           VARIANCE(r.AREA) AS area_variance\\n    FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY d\\n    JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION o ON d.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\\n    JOIN FCLT_ROOMS r ON o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = r.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\\n    WHERE d.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL\\n      AND r.AREA > 40\\n    GROUP BY o.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n),\\nunit_stats AS (\\n    SELECT c.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n           AVG(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units,\\n           MAX(c.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range,\\n           VARIANCE(c.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance\\n    FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED c\\n    JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t ON c.TERM_CODE = t.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE t.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y'\\n    GROUP BY c.DEPARTMENT_NAME\\n)\\nSELECT rs.DEPARTMENT_NAME,\\n       rs.avg_area,\\n       rs.area_range,\\n       rs.area_variance,\\n       us.avg_total_units,\\n       us.total_units_range,\\n       us.total_units_variance\\nFROM room_stats rs\\nJOIN unit_stats us ON rs.DEPARTMENT_NAME = us.DEPARTMENT_NAME\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
